  "scenarios": [
    "Actual curl loopback named, unnamed and malformed-body incomplete events preserve ProviderError body/diagnostic and issue exactly one request; existing cancellation/transport-retry tests retained",
    "Read-only normalization of legacy empty Anthropic wire arrays, deferred-commit failure, next save before reload, resume, compaction and provider switching",
    "Large provider states above 8 MiB use zero unchanged-payload-row reads, changed-suffix serialization, external-change invalidation and owning/nested rollback checks",
    "Missing and malformed recovery archives preserve original references and unknown outcomes, reconstruct available journal facts, retain multiple distinct missing records, survive forks and permit new turns without repeating effects",
    "Ordinary and summary requests receive fresh execution facts outside the system prompt; oversized snapshots replace one private file, retain a digest and create no permanent reference rows; legacy system snapshots receive an explicit empty update",
    "Failed checkpoint publication removes its newly created unreferenced recovery candidate; immutable historical archives remain retained",
    "Rejected preview retains a relative reference through save/reload, relocation and later compaction",
    "Three 5 KiB command results execute exactly once each under the bounded batch budget; protected page and oversized-input safeguards retained",
    "Shared two-summary budget reports exhaustion accurately and stops a new checkpoint attempt",
    "Repair inspection makes no session-row changes; explicit repair backs up raw data, preserves malformed UTF-8 bytes, rolls back after backup on SQL failure, preserves journals and makes no provider requests",
    "Failed reply persistence preserves a private uncommitted receipt and never dispatches its calls",
    "New capture first flushes and at-capacity closes perform zero ordinary catalog scans; catalog corruption, lock, quota and unsafe-sidecar tests retained"
  ],
